# comptime_fields.tkr — the §14 B5 ACCEPT host: Family-B comptime FIELD reflection (Extent-3, GUARDED).
# A `@fields<T>()` call folds to a `[]FieldInfo` comptime aggregate — one DESCRIPTOR (name + nullability)
# per field of `T`, in declaration order, projected from the checker's field view. DESCRIPTORS ONLY: it
# never reads any instance's runtime field value (Law M.0 / §14.2). Each scenario names itself and
# asserts its announced value through `run`/`run_str` in `main.tks`, so a relapse names itself.

Feature: comptime_fields — Family-B comptime field reflection (§14 B5)

  Scenario: fields_count — @fields<Point>() has 2 descriptors (x, y)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario fields_count: ok"

  Scenario: fields_name0 — @fields<Point>()[0].name is "x"
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario fields_name0: ok"

  Scenario: fields_name1 — @fields<Point>()[1].name is "y"
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario fields_name1: ok"

  Scenario: fields_nullable_false — @fields<Nub>()[0] (a: i64) is not nullable
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario fields_nullable_false: ok"

  Scenario: fields_nullable_true — @fields<Nub>()[1] (b: i64 | null) is nullable
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario fields_nullable_true: ok"
